This section supersedes the Fix Round 1/2 cleanup and cross-worker claims called out above. Verified absence now means a successful, empty query for the already-known full container ID without a label predicate. Typed status failures and exceptions remain secondary evidence, and an active candidate/controller primary carries all cleanup evidence in exception notes.

### Files changed in Fix Round 3

- `agent_loop.py`
  - Checks `timed_out` and nonzero `returncode` for every daemon kill/wait/rm result while continuing all later actions.
  - Verifies final absence by the known full container ID alone.
  - Records typed secondary error messages on active acquired-session primaries while preserving their original type/message; explicit close retains its existing raised cleanup failure.
- `core/pit_optimizer_candidate.py`
  - Restricts the only allowed `.append` receiver to an exact single-bound local `ast.Name`; attribute/subscript/nested receivers are rejected.
- `tests/test_agent_loop.py`
