`python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_agent_loop.py -k "hostile_returncode or hostile_result_getter or hostile_result_to_generic"`

RED result against unchanged production code: **4 failed, 518 deselected**.
The hostile return-code comparison, hostile `timed_out` getter, hostile final
`stdout` getter, and hostile timeout truth test each escaped from cleanup at the
reviewed field-use boundary and stopped later owner cleanup.

GREEN result after the exact-shape normalization change: same command,
**4 passed, 518 deselected**. The hostile scalar methods and subclass getters
were not invoked. The two malformed-protocol cases retained the identical
exception object observed at the session-close boundary, exact `ValueError`
type and message, and only bounded closed-code notes. Explicit close returned
the exact generic cleanup `SandboxError`; a second close remained idempotent
only after the first attempted every action and removed the package tree.

Combined prior/new cleanup regression:

`python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_agent_loop.py -k "cleanup_evidence or cleanup_faults_preserve_primary or explicit_close_reports or policy_daemon_cleanup_checks_status or hostile_returncode or hostile_result_getter or hostile_result_to_generic"`

